<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Editor: Ladder Collider Checks (~10 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~10 min</span>
    </div>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Editor / Code Fix</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Falls right before reaching the upper platform</td>
            <td>Trigger box stops slightly below the floor collider top edge</td>
            <td>Extend the ladder <code>BoxCollider2D</code> slightly above the upper ledge so <code>OnTriggerExit2D()</code> runs only after your feet clear the edge.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Touching two stacked ladders drops the player halfway up</td>
            <td>Exiting ladder #1 runs <code>OnTriggerExit2D()</code> and sets <code>isPlatformer = true</code> while still inside ladder #2</td>
            <td>Use <em>one</em> tall ladder trigger per shaft instead of stacking separate triggers on top of each other.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Player cannot jump right after stepping off a ladder onto thin platforms</td>
            <td>Still touching side wall or missed <code>"Ground"</code> collision</td>
            <td>Confirm the landing ledge carries the <code>Ground</code> tag and solid collider so <code>OnCollisionEnter2D()</code> refills <code>jumpsRemaining</code>.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Collider Geometry &amp; Level Flow</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Why is one scaled <code>BoxCollider2D</code> safer than three stacked <code>Ladder</code> trigger objects inside the same vertical shaft?</li>
            <li>What happens if you jump past a decorative ladder that sits in the background behind a main combat jump? Should decorative art carry the <code>Ladder</code> tag or remain untagged without a trigger?</li>
            <li>How does combining a ladder shaft, a moving <code>Platform</code>, and a <code>TurretController</code> teach a player what skills they will need in your upcoming boss fight?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

